# Tasks (agile-md)

A filesystem Kanban managed by the `amd` command.
Status is the folder; `git mv` between columns is the audit trail.

Columns: {% for column in columns %}`{{ column }}/`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
Each task is `{{ board }}/<column>/NNN-slug.md`.

There is one kind of ticket; what varies is its labels. `type`
({% for kind in types %}`{{ kind }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
is also the branch prefix — `amd start` switches to `<type>/<title>` — and
`epic` groups tasks across the board (`amd epics`).

Tasks are rendered from a Jinja template. Run `amd templates` to see what's
available, and `amd templates eject task` to drop an editable copy into
`{{ board }}/templates/` — anything there overrides the built-ins.

See https://github.com/mrdoodles/agile-md
